  "reason": "The dominant finding is that scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder drives a massive accuracy jump (0.725 in config_039 vs ~0.51-0.52 for scgpt configs), making it the clear backbone. The best config (config_039) uses weighted fusion; the only other scgpt comparison (config_016 vs config_036) showed weighted slightly beating concat, but that was with a weaker RNA encoder. Config_028 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) isolates the fusion method while holding all other components at the best-known values. This tells us whether weighted fusion provides a genuine advantage over concat when the RNA representation is already strong, or whether the ~0.01 gap seen with scgpt was noise. With 5 experiments remaining, understanding which components are truly load-bearing is critical before committing budget to further modifications. If concat matches weighted, it simplifies the search space; if weighted clearly wins, it confirms config_039's fusion choice and we can focus remaining experiments on other axes (aggregation, image encoder)."
}

